. Every","+number carries its size range and the section whose regenerate command","+produces it; the status of every claim is **theorem** (a Lean name under","+`lean/MOSPFormalization/`, no `sorry`, axioms `propext`, `Classical.choice`,","+`Quot.sound` only), **certified** (a file under","+`reports/scratch/obstruction_search/`, verified by `paper1/obstruction_check.py`,","+which shares no code with the searches), or **measured** (a size range, a","+budget and a command). Sections 1–9 are the items, in order, each with its","+tables in full; §10 is this write-up, the paper's paragraph and the paragraph","+drafted for `CLAUDE.md`."," ","+### 0.1 The question, and the correction it rests on","+","+Every certified optimum in this project is a sandwich: a witness layout above,","+found by a tuned search over orderings, and a refutation below. The lower","+bounds that start the descent — the trivial bound, the clique bound,","+contraction degeneracy + 1, Harper's expansion bound at a cap, the greedy","+contraction-minor step — were only ever *computed*: one formula, one greedy","+rule, one budget each. This loop ran a real search over each family of","+lower-bound obstruction on instances whose optimum is already on record, so","+that nothing is solved twice and every answer is a measurement, and reports","+each family's **duality gap**, `optimum − best certified value`, in optimum","+units (`pathwidth + 1`) throughout.","+","+The correction (plan §0.2) is that two of the brief's five families are","+*universal* statements, not maximisations. Harper's bound is","+`pw ≥ min_{|A|=t} |N[A]| − t` for every `t` (Harper 1966;","+`exists_closedNbhd_card_le`, **theorem**), a minimum over **all** `t`-sets; the","+empty-pair bound `n − 2s* − 2 ≤ pw` is its weakening at one `t`","+(`card_sub_two_mul_emptyPairIndex_sub_two_le_pathwidth`, **theorem**). A set","+found by search proves only `f(t) ≤ |N[C]|`, so its value is a **ceiling** on","+what the family could ever certify and is not a bound at all; the valid","+**floor** needs the inner minimum proved, by branch and bound to a cap or by a","+SAT refutation with a DRAT proof. Cliques, contraction minors and separator","+branches are genuine maximisations, and a found object is a certificate.","+Measured before anything was stated: on the 4,123 corpus instances at","+`n ≤ 22`, where the profile `f` is enumerated exactly, the search's ceiling","+equals the exact bound on 4,123 of 4,123 and the exact bound equals the","+optimum on 2,933 (71.1%) (§2).","+","+### 0.2 The families, the direction of each, and the headline on the 338","+","+The 338 bound-gap instances are those where the solver's own `lb_best` misses","+the optimum by two or more (20–134 customers; 102 Chu & Stuckey). The best","+floor **on record** before the loop (`floor0`: `lb_best`, exact treewidth + 1,","+Harper at cap 12, Lemma P, the minor certificates on file) was tight on 81 of","+them; the harness's reference `max(lb_best, tw + 1)` on 67 (§1).","+","+| family | object | a search gives | floor on the 338 (tight / 338) | ceiling on the 338 | certificate, checker | theorem |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| **E** (expansion: Harper, the empty pair) | `f(t) = min_{|C|=t} |N[C]|` | a **ceiling**; incumbents for the exact half | 12 (cap-12 branch and bound, exact enumeration, SAT with DRAT; §2–§3) | **below the optimum on 320 of 338**: the family cannot close them under any computation (§2) | the CNF's hash and a DRAT proof per level; the checker regenerates the CNF, compares the hash, runs `drat-trim`; 158 of 158 verified (§3) | `exists_closedNbhd_card_le`; `pathwidth_ge_of_unsat` (§9) |","+| **M** (contraction minors) | a contraction sequence | a **floor**: the minor's proved width | **327** (324 by the search or the greedy ladder, 3 by the record's certificates; §4–§5, §8) | the optimum, trivially | the sequence, the minor's edge hash, the C program's output and binary hash; the checker replays with its own code, re-prove