 (364 vertices): the branch lemma down the tree as a nested","+B certificate (121 `branch` nodes, 243 `trivial` leaves), `pw ≥ 5` = the","+layout's width, verified with no C call — the value is Ellis, Sudborough &","+Turner (1994)'s, the certificate is new to the record. `NY_13` (PACE 2017,","+283 vertices, width 10, floor 9): the minor search found an **85-vertex","+contraction minor of pathwidth 10** (refutes 9 in 67,455 nodes, 0.07 s;","+236.7 core-hours on the whole graph had found nothing), verified on all three","+checks including the rule-free one — `pw(NY_13) = 10`. On 21 of the other 22","+family M's floor is `width − 1` (`width − 2` on `494_bus`), each a C","+refutation on a minor at 30–39% of the vertices; five floors rose above the","+record (2 → 7, 3 → 9, 2 → 8, 3 → 9, 9 → 10). **Harper's ceiling is below the","+recorded width on all 24** (by 1–5): the expansion family cannot close any of","+them. 47 of 47 certificates verified. The evidence rows are written in","+`paper1.dataset`'s run format and the `OPEN_RUNS` addition is **proposed, not","+applied** (`07_open/open_runs_proposal.diff`): with the `NY_13` row, `fold`","+would emit a new `certified:minor` record, i.e. a dataset rebuild, which the","+loop forbids (§7).","+","+### 0.4 What no family closes","+","+**375 of 6,376 (5.9%)**: 370 at gap 1 and **5 at gap ≥ 2**, the five all","+`Random-125-125-4/6`. 302 of the 375 lie at excess `e ≤ 3.30`, three deciles","+holding 30% of the corpus; tightness rises with the excess for every family","+(E's floor from 30% to 98% across deciles, `floor0` from 66% to 100%). On","+every one of the 222 searched uncovered instances E's ceiling is below the","+optimum, so the expansion family can close none of them under any","+computation; family M ran on 11 of the 375 (the 338's residual), and","+\"uncovered\" means uncovered *on record*: at 9–60 customers M was tight on","+every instance it ran on, and the 364 gap-1 instances outside the 338 were","+never given a floor-producing search (§8.5). The ten smallest uncovered","+(9–10 customers, drawn in `08_map/tables.md`) are hubs with a fringe, the","+bound-defeating family `CLAUDE.md`'s bounds section describes — an","+observation on ten matrices, not a claim about the 375.","+","+### 0.5 The kill verdicts (plan §0.9)","+","+| family | criterion | the number | verdict |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| E, the search | `f̂(t) = f(t)` at every `t` on < 90% at `n ≤ 22` | 4,090 of 4,123 (99.2%) | **not met** (§2) |","+| E, the exact half | SAT settles the argmax level on < 50% of the 338 within 6 core-hours | 70 of 338 (20.7%); 70 of the 145 with a bracket (48.3%) | **met**: Harper exact is out of reach by SAT above cap 12 at 75 customers and beyond, fully in reach to 60; the boundary is `n ≈ 60–75` at `t* ≈ 0.2–0.35 n` on the Chu & Stuckey graphs (§3) |","+| M | the search beats the greedy ladder on < 10% of the 338 | 45 of 338 (13.3%) | **not met**, by a small margin: never by more than one at `n ≤ 60`, and the ladder costs a hundredth of the time (§4.3, §5) |","+| B | no B certificate exceeds `max(lb_best, tw + 1, M)` on any residual gap instance | 0 of 11; 0 of 338 | **met**: branching is closed (§6) |","+| open classes | zero floors above the recorded ones (the tree aside) is a verdict | 5 of 23 floors above the record; 2 of 24 closed | **not met** (§7) |","+| Lean | a statement false to 8 vertices is corrected before it is stated | 2 corrected, 0 stated unchecked | **met** (§9) |","+","+No stop condition fired in any item: no bound on record above a certified","+optimum (6,376 × 9 columns, §1), no dataset floor above a certified width","+(16,636 × 4), no certificate the checker rejects that the record relies on","+(the three rejections of §4.1 were bugs in the checker, fixed and tested),","+no floor above an open class's width, no statement false on a small graph","+committed.","+","+### 0.6 The certificates, their checkers and the Lean theorems","+","+Five certificate kinds, one checker (`paper1/obstruction_check.py`,","+sub-commands `check-expansion`, `check-minor`, `check-branch`; own readers,","+own graph, own CNF generator, own contraction replay, own BFS; no import","+from `learning/`, `satisfiability/`, `pathwidth_solver/` or `mosp/`). Every","+certificate the report cites went through it, and the verdict is in the","+item's `checker_verdicts.csv`: 158 of 158 (E, §3), 251 of 251 (M at","+`n ≤ 60`, §4), 190 of 190 (M at scale and the ridge, §5), 156 of 156 (B, §6),","+47 of 47 (the open classes, §7). The DRAT proofs (1.3 GB) are git-ignored","+and regenerable; their hashes are committed. Every floor went through","+`learning/bound_harness.py`'s validity stage on all 6,376: \"above optimum\"","+**0** for each of `harper_floor`, the SAT floor, the M floor and the B floor.","+","+What the checker's verdict rests on, now stated in Lean","+(`ObstructionCertificate.lean`, 22 theorems, no `sorry`, no `axiom`; §9):","+an UNSAT level `(t, b)` gives `b + 1 ≤ t + pw` (`pathwidth_ge_of_unsat`,","+needing `t ≤ n`; its omission is a proved counterexample); a contraction","+sequence whose minor has minimum degree `d` gives `d ≤ pw`","+(`pathwidth_ge_of_minor_minDegree`; the degree form needs a nonempty minor,","+likewise); the `Bool` replay `checkSeq` is sound and complete; and three","+certificates are closed by `decide`, among them the record instance","+`Warwick 1729` (30 customers): **every pattern order opens at least 8","+stacks** (`eight_le_mospValue_warwick`, 7.6 s in `lake build`, directly on","+the MOSP graph Lean builds from the matrix). A finding on the way: the C","+program's `bound` status reports the minor's *contraction degeneracy*, not","+its minimum degree, so the 39 `bound` certificates of §4–§5 do not exhibit","+the object the theorem needs without the MMD+ contractions behind the","+status; emitting them is **proposed, not applied** (§9.3). A C-program","+*refutation* on a minor or a branch rests, as before, on `Search/`'s","+soundness theorems and the binary's faithfulness.","+","+### 0.7 The cost ledger","+","+Regenerated from the items' own seconds columns (`08_map/cost.csv`, §8.7):","+**about 35 core-hours** (32.51 instance + 0.96 checker in the files, about","+1.4 more in the logs' uncounted harness, validation and smoke runs) against","+the plan's 56 — E 9.7 (§1–§3, and §7's 0.5), M 15.7 (§4–§5) and 5.75 (§7),","+B 0.5 and 0.4, the open classes 7.1 in all; every process at `nice -n 19`,","+at most 8 workers, under the owner's load of 1–59. Sessions (`loop.log`,","+`session_it*.log`): items 01–09 in twelve sessions including two gate-fix","+sessions, 2026-11-02 21:42 to 2026-11-03 10:47 (13.1 h wall), **$193.18**","+over the ten sessions whose logs carry a cost line (the capped fix session","+and this session excluded). The gate's test count rose from 1,804 to 1,890","+in `tests/` (seven new test modules), 123 in `pathwidth_solver/` unchanged;","+the paper stays at 77 pages. Nothing under `solutions/` was touched and no","+whole proved graph was re-solved.","+","+### 0.8 What is open","+","+1. The 11 of the 338, and the 5 at gap ≥ 2: dense 100–125-customer Chu &","+   Stuckey instances where every family stops one to four stacks short of","+   an optimum the search proves only by exhausting `10¹¹` nodes.","+2. `Random-125-125-2-2_0`: no minor certificate for 25 at any size tried","+   (greedy to 95 on record, 97–110 here); whether one exists is open.","+3. Harper's exact floor above 75 customers at the argmax levels (§3's","+   boundary); the SAT route is closed there, and no other exact route was","+   tried.","+4. Twenty-two open classes with family M's floor at `width − 1`: either a","+   larger minor refutes `width − 1` or the stored layout is one too high.","+5. Two proposals for the owner: the MMD+ contractions behind a `bound`","+   status (§9.3), and the `OPEN_RUNS` line that would fold `NY_13` into the","+   dataset (§7.4); a 97–99% rung for the ladder (§5).","+6. `decide` on the 100–125-customer certificates, and a decidable form of","+   the branch certificate (§9.4): not tried.","+7. The reserve (item 11): F5, combinations of families, or the best","+   remaining gap above.","+","+### 0.9 What this does not claim","+","+That any family closes the 11; that family E's ceiling is attained by any","+computation (it is an upper bound on the family's reach, measured by a","+search of stated budget); that a searched minor for `2-2_0` does not exist;","+that the greedy ladder is near-optimal among minors (it is one short on 29","+of 251 at `n ≤ 60`); that anything here changes the solver (no candidate","+reaches `_lower_bound` or any path that decides `k`; the expansion bound's","+net loss *inside the search* is about the solver's clock and untouched);","+that the dataset is rebuilt (it is not; two closed classes are filed as","+evidence rows and certificates). \"We found no prior report\" of a searched","+contraction-minor or searched vertex-isoperimetric lower bound for pathwidth","+on benchmark instances; never \"first\". The pathwidth of trees is Ellis,","+Sudborough & Turner (1994); Harper's bound is Harper (1966).","+"," ---"," "," ## 1. The baseline ledger and the frozen targets (item 01)"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/obstruction_search.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015yv9ZMRRX1ynm2DwGUDRz2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
