leaf; 156 of 156 verified (§6) | `branch_lemma_separator`, `branch_lemma` |","-| **C, D, T, P** (on record) | cliques; `lb_best`; `tw + 1`; pendant cliques | — | 0 / 67 / 67 / 3 alone or tied (§1, §8) | — | — | `card_le_pathwidth_add_one_of_isClique`, `degeneracy_le_pathwidth`, `treewidth_le_pathwidth`, `pathwidth_ge_of_pendant_cliques` |","+| **C, D, T, P** (on record) | cliques; `lb_best`; `tw + 1`; pendant cliques | — | 0 / 0 (by the definition of the 338) / 67 / 0 (P is above `lb_best` on 3, by one) (§1, §8) | — | — | `card_le_pathwidth_add_one_of_isClique`, `degeneracy_le_pathwidth`, `treewidth_le_pathwidth`, `pathwidth_ge_of_pendant_cliques` |"," "," **The best floor over every family is tight on 327 of the 338 and on 6,001"," of the 6,376 corpus instances (94.1%; `floor0` 5,732, 89.9%), and every one"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/obstruction_search.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NKGoa7dNLSLzaksQ1ZSHyq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgfsJAU4NEQCXQT85So97","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DKrEjpwzSZ5ywzYfvQLyd8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='paper1/latex/sec5_results.tex'\ns=open(p).read()\nanchor=\"trees are too large to ship as certificates.\\n\\n\\\\subsection{A dataset with certified pathwidth}\"\nassert s.count(anchor)==1\npara=r\"\"\"trees are too large to ship as certificates.\n\n\\paragraph{Searched lower bounds, with certificates.} The witness half of\nevery certified value is found by a tuned search over orderings. The lower\nbounds that start the descent, the clique, contraction degeneracy, Harper's\nvertex-isoperimetric bound at a cap \\citep{Harper1966} and the greedy minor\nstep of Section~\\ref{sec:minor}, were only ever computed, one formula or one\ngreedy rule each. We ran a search over each family of obstruction on\ninstances whose optimum is known, so that every answer is a measurement, and\nreport the family's duality gap, the optimum minus the best value it\ncertifies. Two kinds of family must be told apart. Harper's bound is\nuniversal, $\\pw\\ge\\min_{|A|=t}|N[A]|-t$ for every $t$, so a set found by\nsearch proves only that the minimum is at most its value: it gives a\n\\emph{ceiling} on what the family could ever certify and no bound at all, and\nthe floor needs the minimum proved, by branch and bound to a cap or by a SAT\nrefutation with a DRAT proof. Cliques, contraction minors and separator\nbranches are maximisations, and a found object is a certificate. Each\ncertificate has a format and an independent checker sharing no code with the\nsearch: it regenerates the CNF of an expansion level and runs\n\\texttt{drat-trim}; replays a contraction sequence with its own code, rebuilds\nthe minor, re-runs our search on it and, to 80 vertices, a rule-free\nenumeration of refuted prefixes; checks a separator's branches by its own\nbreadth-first search. That a verified certificate implies the bound is proved\nin Lean, and \\texttt{decide} closes a 30-customer record instance from its\nown matrix~\\leanref{obstruction}.\n\nOn the 338 instances of the MOSP corpus where the solver's own bound misses\nthe optimum by two or more (20 to 134 customers), the best floor on record was\ntight on 81. Searched contraction minors, each refuted on the minor by our\ncorrected search under a cap of 2 to 10\\,s per call, are tight on 327: at 20\nto 50 customers on 251 of 251, beating the greedy ladder of\nSection~\\ref{sec:minor} on 29, always by one; above 60 customers on 76 of 87.\nThey reach 93 on \\texttt{Random-125-125-8-2\\_0}, its optimum, on a 118-customer\nminor, and shrink the minor that certifies \\texttt{Random-125-125-2-3\\_0} from\n70 customers to 51, refuting 20 in 145,355 nodes; no minor of up to 110\ncustomers certifies \\texttt{Random-125-125-2-2\\_0} within one core-hour.\nHarper's ceiling is below the optimum on 320 of the 338, so no computation of\nthat bound could close them; its exact floor, by SAT with a checked DRAT\nproof, settles every bracket at 30 to 60 customers and almost none at 75 and\nbeyond, and closes 12. Separator branches close none. The 11 instances left\nare dense Chu and Stuckey instances at 100 to 125 customers with the best\nfloor one to four stacks below the optimum. Of the dataset's 24 open classes\n(Section~\\ref{sec:dataset}), two are closed by certificates filed with the\ncode (the dataset's records are unchanged): the complete ternary tree of\nheight 5 by the branch lemma, at the pathwidth that \\citet{EllisSudboroughTurner1994}\ncompute for trees, and the PACE instance \\texttt{NY\\_13} (283 vertices, width\n10) by an 85-vertex contraction minor of pathwidth 10, refuted in 0.07\\,s\nwhere 236.7 core-hours on the whole graph had found nothing. Harper's ceiling\nis below the recorded width on all 24. Every certificate verifies: 158\nexpansion levels, 441 minors, 156 separators and 47 on the open classes, at\nabout 35 core-hours in all. We found no prior report of a searched\ncontraction-minor or searched vertex-isoperimetric lower bound on benchmark\ninstances. The searches, the checker and the certificates are in the\nrepository (Section~\\ref{sec:data}).\n\n\\subsection{A dataset with certified pathwidth}\"\"\"\ns=s.replace(anchor,para); open(p,'w').write(s); print('sec5 ok')\n\np='paper1/latex/sec9a_appendix_lean.tex'\ns=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('\\\\leanentry{obstruction}')\nj=s.index('\\\\\\\\\\n',i)+3\nold=s[i:j]\nnew=(r\"\"\"\\leanentry{obstruction}{A checked lower-bound certificate implies the bound (Section~\\ref{sec:certs}): an UNSAT expansion level $(t,b)$ with $t\\le n$ gives $b+1\\le t+\\pw$ (Harper's bound, contrapositive; the hypothesis $t\\le n$ is necessary, one-vertex counterexample); a legal contraction sequence whose minor has minimum degree $d$ gives $d\\le\\pw$, in the \\texttt{minDegreeIn} form and in the degree form on a nonempty minor (necessary, likewise); the \\texttt{Bool} replay \\path{checkSeq} is sound and complete for legal sequences; both in MOSP units} \\leannames{pathwidth_ge_of_forall_closedNbhd, pathwidth_ge_of_unsat, pathwidth_ge_of_forall_closedNbhd_needs_le, mospValue_ge_of_unsat, checkSeq_sound, checkSeq_complete, checkSeq_iff, pathwidth_ge_of_minor_minDegree, pathwidth_ge_of_checkSeq, degree_minorOf_eq, pathwidth_ge_of_minor_forall_degree, pathwidth_ge_of_minor_forall_degree_needs_nonempty, mospValue_ge_of_minor_minDegree} \\\\\n\\leanentry{obstruction-decided}{Three certificates closed by \\texttt{decide}: the 8-cycle contracted to a triangle ($2\\le\\pw$), $K_{3,4}$ at level one over all 128 subsets ($3\\le\\pw$), and the record instance \\emph{Warwick 1729} (30 customers, 90 requirements), whose 22-step contraction sequence to $K_8$ is replayed on the MOSP graph Lean builds from the matrix: every pattern order opens at least 8 stacks (optimum 9)} \\leannames{two_le_pathwidth_octGraph, 